    "description": {
      "classificationDescription": "Mt. Tagapo is classified as a minor climb due to its low elevation, short hiking duration, and non-technical nature. The trail does not require specialized mountaineering skills or equipment, and the summit can be reached through a manageable trek. These characteristics make the mountain accessible to a wide range of hikers, particularly those seeking an introductory hiking experience.",
      "lascoRatingDescription": "Mt. Tagapo is assigned a 2/10 difficulty rating because it features a relatively short and straightforward trail with gradual ascents and well-defined paths. The hike can typically be completed within a few hours and does not involve significant elevation gain, technical climbing, or challenging terrain. Most sections consist of easy trekking, making it suitable for beginners and hikers with limited experience."
    },
