    "general": {
      "active": true,
      "address": "Talim Island, Binangonan, Rizal",
      "description": "Mt. Tagapo is a beginner-friendly minor climb rated 2/9 in difficulty that stands as the highest point on Talim Island in Binangonan, Rizal. Commonly accessed via a multi-step journey from Manila that involves a passenger boat crossing across Laguna de Bay to Barangay Janosa, the standard day hike takes about 3 to 4.5 hours to complete. The trail begins with an easy, partially shaded walk passing through a local residential matrix, wooded areas, and bamboo trails before transitioning onto an open cogon grassland upper slope. While technically manageable with no specialized gear or technical scrambling required, the route presents real challenges in the form of intense heat exposure, high island humidity, a steeper final summit push, and a lack of reliable water sources on the trail. Tourism infrastructure at the jump-off includes basic registration facilities near the barangay basketball court, local guides, toilets, wash-up areas, and small sari-sari stores, while overnight camping is permitted at a designated site located roughly 10 to 15 minutes below the exposed summit.",
      "guidelines": [
        "Bonfires are not allowed to avoid grass fire.",
        "Leave No Trace (LNT) should be practiced when hiking."
      ],
      "lgu_rules": [
        "Camping in the summit is prohibited."
      ],
      "mountain": [
