    "description": {
      "classificationDescription": "Mt. Daraitan is classified as a minor climb because it has a relatively low elevation of approximately 739 MASL, can usually be completed within a day, and does not require specialized climbing equipment or advanced mountaineering skills. Although the terrain is more rugged than many beginner mountains, its elevation, accessibility, and hiking duration align with the characteristics of a minor climb.",
      "lascoRatingDescription": "Mt. Daraitan is rated 4/9 because it features steep ascents, rocky limestone terrain, narrow trails, river crossings, and sections that require light scrambling and the use of hands for balance. While the hike is physically demanding and requires good endurance, it remains manageable as a day hike and does not involve advanced technical mountaineering. These conditions make it moderately challenging, placing it within the 4/9 difficulty range."
